Third-party notices for the TwinOak repeater firmware
=====================================================

The firmware itself is MIT (LICENSE). A release of it also carries one file
nobody here built: the base under the application on a RAK4630 - the MBR, the
SoftDevice S140 6.1.1 and the bootloader, as one Intel HEX
(twinoak-base-rak4630-<bootloader version>-s140-6.1.1.hex, `use: provision`
in manifest.json; boards/base/rak4630/README.md says where it came from and
what it is). The notices its licences ask for follow. This file is part of
every release, beside the manifest.

The firmware is built on MeshCore (https://github.com/meshcore-dev/MeshCore),
MIT, which is a pinned dependency and not vendored (docs/upstream.md); the one
file of its tree copied here, boards/rak4631.json, is under that licence.


